# Example user CLAUDE.md  (user scope)

This is an example of a personal, cross-project instruction file. It does NOT belong in this repo.
It lives in your home folder and applies to every project you open with Claude Code.

Install it:

    cp docs/user-CLAUDE.md.example  ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md

Everything below the line is the file content. These are personal preferences (your taste and your
tools), not project rules, so they belong at user scope, not in a project CLAUDE.md.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

# My preferences (all projects)

## Style
- Keep answers concise. Show the diff, not a lecture.
- Explain your plan before a large or multi-file refactor. I want to review first.

## Tools
- Use `rg` (ripgrep) instead of `grep`, and `fd` instead of `find`.
- Prefer `python -m venv` for Python environments.

## Habits
- After you finish a task, run the project's tests and report pass or fail.
- When you fix the same kind of bug twice, tell me so I can add it to the project's CLAUDE.md.
